Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

REQ-CONDUCTOR-FINISHED-1. Origin: exp6901 (2026-09-02). _artifact_is_finished
checked status in _BOOTSTRAP_STATUSES before the verdict; the set contains
"blocked", so the honest terminal verdict complete_blocked_* read as an
unfinished skeleton. The conductor re-ran the task twice more (each rerun
reproduced the identical blocked artifact; the third died at the 4803s
wall-clock cap), logged 3x FAIL artifact_not_updated_past_bootstrap, retired
the task, and pre-emptively skipped exp6902-6904. Seven tasks repeated the
pattern in two weeks (exp6753/6765/6773/6784/6796/6837/6901 — 3 FAILs each).

The verdict classifier already settled the policy this check was defeating:
terminal-prefixed verdicts are trusted (2026-05-05, exp1305), and bare
blocked_<resource> is trusted (2026-05-27, the .294 incident — "no retry can
change that"; the Pre-Launch Preconditions Discipline says such a task
"simply retires"). The status-first check silenced both whenever the agent
also wrote status: "blocked" — the natural pairing. exp6898 wrote
status=complete_blocked and logged OK the same day exp6901 wrote
status=blocked and burned 3 runs; the only difference was the status string.

Fix: for status == "blocked" ONLY, consult _verdict_is_untrustworthy first;
a trustworthy non-empty verdict marks the artifact finished. Rejected shapes:
skeletons (status blocked, no verdict) still re-run; partial verdicts still
re-run; status running/in_progress/partial keep the strict path, so the
exp1028 pre-written-conclusion hole stays closed. _deliverable_exists is
deliberately unchanged — its strict check is the recovery path when a
re-proposed task reuses a deliverable path, and the fail-safe direction on
that fast path is toward re-running.

Considered and not built: wiring _classify_retirement (dead since May) or a
respawn queue consumer. The classifier-first check is smaller and addresses
both harms at once (the rerun burn AND the FAIL-count retirement), because a
finished artifact takes the normal OK completion path.

Corpus survey: 13 artifacts corpus-wide carry a bootstrap status plus a
terminal-prefixed verdict; 593 carry status blocked plus bare blocked_*.
Zero of the 7 incident tasks were rescued by a same-milestone retry.

6 tests; mutations: override disabled -> RED, empty-verdict requirement
dropped -> RED, scope widened past "blocked" -> RED; restored byte-identical
(cmp). Verified against the real exp6901/6753/6784 artifacts: all now read
finished. Takes effect at the conductor's next re-exec on fresh source.

